@startuml
title State diagram for Healthcare Portal

[*] --> Registration

state Registration {
    state "New User" as NewUser
    state "Registered User" as RegisteredUser
}

' New user registration
NewUser : entry / Start
NewUser : do / Enter details
NewUser : exit / Validate details
RegisteredUser : entry / Successful Registration
RegisteredUser : do / Access granted
RegisteredUser : exit / Login

Registration --> NewUser : User is new
NewUser --> RegisteredUser : Details are valid

' Failed registration
NewUser --> [*] : Details are invalid

Login : entry / To Action
Login : do / Log in to the system
Login : exit / Username and password entered

[*] --> Login
Login --> SignIn : Correct login details
SignIn : entry / Access granted
SignIn : do / Provide access to facilities
SignIn : exit / Continue using the system

' Failed sign in
SignIn --> [*] : Incorrect login details

Facilities : entry / To Action
Facilities : do / Read news and expert content
Facilities : do / Check symptoms or use fitness checking options
Facilities : exit / View result

Result : entry / To Action
Result : do / Continue using the system or finish session
Result : exit / Logout

Insurance : entry / To Action
Insurance : do / Process and validate insurance
Insurance : do / Check payment with insurance for doctor consultations
Insurance : do / Complete the payment process

Payment : entry / To Action
Payment : do / Allow users to select payment methods (cash or insurance)
Payment : do / Inform users about cash payment details if chosen as the payment method
Payment : do / Complete the payment process for insurance-based payments

Feedback : entry / To Action
Feedback : do / Collect user feedback after service completion

Logout : entry / To Action
Logout : do / Log out users at the end of their session

SignIn --> Insurance : Requires finance-related services
Insurance --> Payment : Requires payment
Payment --> Feedback : After service completion
Feedback --> Logout : At the end of the session
@enduml
